<title>USA: U.S. Xpress CFO Bentley resigns.</title>
<headline>U.S. Xpress CFO Bentley resigns.</headline>
<dateline>CHATTANOOGA, Tenn. 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Xpress Enterprises Inc said Thursday Larry Bentley will resign as its director, executive vice president and chief financial officer, effective September 13.</p>
<p>The company declined to give a reason for Bentley's resignation.</p>
<p>It said Donald Rutledge, formerly general manager of U.S. Xpress Inc, the company's largest subsidiary, will serve as interim chief financial officer. The company said a nationwide search is underway to select Bentley's successor.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
